{
	"chapters/tips_and_tricks.snbt": {
		quest.47043AF7D1FABC43.quest_desc: {
			new: [
				"There's many ways to extract Enchantments from Items onto Books. This quest will focus on many of such methods.\\n\\n&cSuper Factory Manager&r: One of the cheapest ways I can think of to disenchant your gear, with no &aExperience&r cost whatsoever. Drop your Enchanted Item and a bunch of Books on a block of &5Obsidian&r, then make a falling &8Anvil&r land on top of the Enchanted Item and the Books.\\n\\n&bDis-Enchanting Table&r: Simply put an Enchanted Item in the Left Slot and a Book in the Middle Slot. Then, the Enchants will go to the Right Slot in Book form! Costs &aExperience&r.\\nYou can also use Enchanted Books instead of the Item to split up its Enchantments.\\n\\n&6Draconic Evolution Disenchanter&r: This one lets you choose a specific enchantment from an Enchanted Item to move to a Book. Costs &aExperience&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&cEvilCraft Purifier and Blook&r: Uses &cBlood&r to extract enchantments from an Enchanted Item onto a &cBlook&r.\\n\\n&5&lApothic Enchanting Tomes&r: When used in an anvil, these will extract all enchantments from the Enchanted Item.\\nThe &8Tome of Scrapping&r only extracts half of the enchantments from the Item, destroying that item in the process.\\nThe &8Tome of Superior Scrapping&r extracts all enchantments from the Item, destroying that item in the process.\\nThe &8Tome of Extraction&r extracts all enchantments from the Item, keeping the item in the process.\\nCheck out the &5&lApothic Enchanting&r chapter to learn more about how to infuse these Tomes.\\n\\n&bIndustrial Foregoing Enchantment Extractor&r: Recommended for automated disenchanting. Place an Enchanted Item and Books into the machine, and it will extract Enchantments from the Item. You can also have the enchantments be turned into &aEssence&r instead, if you prefer.\\n\\n&5Actually Additions Lens of Disenchanting&r: These Lens go into an Atomic Reconstructor. Throw an Enchanted Item and a single Book in front of the Laser that the Atomic Reconstructor emits, and it will separate a single Enchantment from the Item onto the Book"
			]
			old: [
				"There's many ways to extract Enchantments from Items onto Books. This quest will focus on many of such methods.\\n\\n&cSuper Factory Manager&r: One of the cheapest ways I can think of to disenchant your gear, with no &aExperience&r cost whatsoever. Drop your Enchanted Item and a bunch of Books on a block of &5Obsidian&r, then make a falling &8Anvil&r land on top of the Enchanted Item and the Books.\\n\\n&bDis-Enchanting Table&r: Simply put an Enchanted Item in the Left Slot and a Book in the Middle Slot. Then, the Enchants will go to the Right Slot in Book form! Costs &aExperience&r.\\nYou can also use Enchanted Books instead of the Item to split up its Enchantments.\\n\\n&6Draconic Evolution Disenchanter&r: This one lets you choose a specific enchantment from an Enchanted Item to move to a Book. Costs &aExperience&r."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"&cEvilCraft Purifier and Blook&r: Uses &cBlood&r to extract enchantments from an Enchanted Item onto a &cBlook&r.\\n\\n&5&lApothic Enchanting Tomes&r: When used in an anvil, these will extract all enchantments from the Enchanted Item.\\nThe &8Tome of Scrapping&r only extracts half of the enchantments from the Item, destroying that item in the process.\\nThe &8Tome of Superior Scrapping&r extracts all enchantments from the Item, destroying that item in the process.\\nThe &8Tome of Extraction&r extracts all enchantments from the Item, keeping the item in the process.\\nCheck out the &5&lApothic Enchanting&r chapter to learn more about how to infuse these Tomes.\\n\\n&bIndustrial Foregoing Enchantment Extractor&r: Recommended for automated disenchanting. Place an Enchanted Item and Books into the machine, and it will extract Enchantments from the Item. You can also have the enchantments be turned into &aEssence&r instead, if you prefer.\\n\\n&8Corail Tombstone Book of Disenchantment&r: Occasionally, Decorative Graves will have a Grave Soul roaming them. You can right click on that Grave Soul with the Book in your offhand and an Enchanted Item in your main hand, and it may strip those enchantments and return them as books. Will corrupt the Grave slightly, so be careful with this method.\\n\\n&5Actually Additions Lens of Disenchanting&r: These Lens go into an Atomic Reconstructor. Throw an Enchanted Item and a single Book in front of the Laser that the Atomic Reconstructor emits, and it will separate a single Enchantment from the Item onto the Book"
			]
		}
	}
	file.snbt: {
		file.0000000000000001.title: {
			new: "All The Mods 10 - Aeronautics Edition"
			old: "All The Mods 10"
		}
	}
	"chapters/mainquestline_part_1.snbt": {
		quest.5792CC9E3AFAB229.quest_desc: {
			new: ["We also have the mod called &eExcessive Utilities&r! This mod adds, among other things, unique generators that use coal or other items."]
			old: ["We also have the mod called &aGenerators Galore&r! This mod adds unique generators that use coal or other items."]
		}
		quest.5CF320E9C4C1B1E1.quest_desc: {
			new: ["ATM10 Aeronautics is a &aKitchensink&r pack, meaning you are free to explore and play the modpack any way that you want!\\n\\nHowever, there is an endgame goal: Making the &6ATM Star&r!\\n\\nThis questline serves as a guide for all players, whether you are brand new to Minecraft or you've played through previous ATM packs.\\n\\nJust like almost every modpack, gather some wood to get started!"]
			old: ["ATM10 is a &aKitchensink&r pack, meaning you are free to explore and play the modpack any way that you want!\\n\\nHowever, there is an endgame goal: Making the &6ATM Star&r!\\n\\nThis questline serves as a guide for all players, whether you are brand new to Minecraft or you've played through previous ATM packs.\\n\\nJust like almost every modpack, gather some wood to get started!"]
		}
		quest.790EC3EDC2DB1FB0.title: {
			new: "More Excessive Utilities Generators"
			old: "Generators Galore"
		}
	}
	"chapters/mi_electric.snbt": {
		quest.1B4CD5AC8F6C3307.quest_desc: {
			new: ["The &#4497DBOverdrive module&r preserves the efficiency of the machine even when the recipe is not currently running. In return, it locks the machine to its current recipe and makes it always use power."]
			old: ["The &#4497DBOverdrive module&r preserves the efficiency of the machine even when the recipe is not currently running. In return it locks the machine for the recipe."]
		}
	}
	"chapters/apotheosis_2.snbt": {
		quest.7F6B66566C211735.quest_desc: {
			new: ["Runes of Debilitation used on the spawner will reduce the max health of the mob spawned. This can decrease their health to as low as 20%"]
			old: ["Dripstone used on the spawner will reduce the max health of the mob spawned. This can decrease their health to as low as 20%"]
		}
		quest.18E0F5A78F696FA3.quest_desc: {
			new: ["Runes of Echoes give a special effect to the spawner. Any mobs spawned will have the loot that they drop multiplied."]
			old: ["Echo shards give a special effect to the spawner. Any mobs spawned will have the loot that they drop multiplied."]
		}
		quest.42D7C8CD8E6F5CD7.quest_desc: {
			new: ["By using a Rune of Stupor on a Spawner you suck the souls out the mobs that will be spawned, only leaving a hollow husk of what they used to be. The mobs will lose all AI so they will do basically what an armor stand does. They can't hit you, can't teleport, can't move on their own. They sit there ready to be killed, how exciting!"]
			old: ["By using a Chorus Fruit on a Spawner you suck the souls out the mobs that will be spawned, only leaving a hollow husk of what they used to be. The mobs will lose all AI so they will do basically what an armor stand does. They can't hit you, can't teleport, can't move on their own. They sit there ready to be killed, how exciting!"]
		}
		quest.30EB438C66324213.quest_desc: {
			new: ["A Rune of Solitude will do part what the Spawner Upgrade Runes do but much better. Players no longer need to be near the spawner. As long as its chunk-loaded it will spawn."]
			old: ["A Nether Star will do what the Prismarine Shards do but much better. Players no longer need to be near the spawner. As long as its chunk-loaded it will spawn."]
		}
		quest.4F7F8F4ED1CA0550.quest_desc: {
			new: ["A Rune of Immolation used on the spawner will have the mobs spawn on fire. Perfect for a nice Steak."]
			old: ["A Campfire used on the spawner will have the mobs spawn on fire. Perfect for a nice Steak."]
		}
		quest.167E1474644C9908.quest_desc: {
			new: ["The Quartz makes whatever the other item does, it does the opposite for the Spawner. With Quartz in your offhand and the other Spawner Modification item in your main it will do the opposite of its role. With Quartz and Runes of Spawning Range instead of increasing Spawn Range it will decrease it. With Quartz and Runes of Debilitation it'll increase Starting Health."]
			old: ["The Quartz makes whatever the other item does, it does the opposite for the Spawner. With Quartz in your offhand and the other Spawner Modification item in your main it will do the opposite of its role. With Quartz and Blaze Rods instead of increasing Spawn Range it will decrease it. With Quartz and Ghast Tears it'll decrease Max Entities."]
		}
		quest.0F89BFD4A3F63A48.quest_desc: {
			new: ["Some mobs (mostly monsters) need certain Light Levels to spawn. Hostile ones needing lower levels and passive needing higher ones. Using a Rune of Perpetual Twilight makes it so you never have to worry about Light Levels as it ignores them! This does not ignore other requirements for spawning like livestock animals needing Grass."]
			old: ["Some mobs (mostly monsters) need certain Light Levels to spawn. Hostile ones needing lower levels and passive needing higher ones. Using a Soul Lantern makes it so you never have to worry about Light Levels as it ignores them! This does not ignore other requirements for spawning like livestock animals needing Grass."]
		}
		quest.6F71FD826C29C31A.quest_desc: {
			new: ["This one might be new to ones returning from earlier versions. By using a Rune of Youth on a Spawner, it will only spawn in baby versions of the mobs in it. This only works with Vanilla baby versions of mobs, not modded."]
			old: ["This one might be new to ones returning from earlier versions. By using a turtle egg on a spawner, it will only spawn in baby versions of the mobs in it. This only works with Vanilla baby versions of mobs, not modded."]
		}
	}
	"chapters/immersive_engineering.snbt": {
		quest.4C4C9ADAC6107F89.quest_desc: {
			new: ["The &eLight Engineering Block&r is pretty easy recipe. \\n\\nYou'll need 1 &6Copper Ingot&r, which I shouldn't have to explain it's literally a &2&lVanilla&r feature. \\n\\n4 &7Iron Sheetmetal&r, which are just 4 &7Iron Plates&r combined with each other! \\n\\nYou'll also need 4 &7Iron Mechanical Components&r, which are either 4 &7Iron Plates&r and a &6Copper Ingot&r in a Crafting Table, or 2 &7Iron Plates&r and a &6Copper Ingot&r in the &6Engineer's Workbench&r."]
			old: ["The &eLight Engineering Block&r is pretty easy recipe. \\n\\nYou'll need 1 &6Copper Ingot&r, which I shouldn't have to explain it's literally a &2&lVanilla&r feature. \\n\\n4 &7Ironsheetmetal&r, which are just 4 &7Iron Plates&r combined with each other! \\n\\nYou'll also need 4 &7Iron Mechanical Components&r, which are either 4 &7Iron Plates&r and a &6Copper Ingot&r in a Crafting Table, or 2 &7Iron Plates&r and a &6Copper Ingot&r in the &6Engineer's Workbench&r."]
		}
	}
	"chapters/basic_power.snbt": {
		quest.0BB367839D28607D.quest_desc: {
			new: ["These &8Coal Generators&r are some of the easiest generators to make.\\n\\nThey are very simple to use and create a decent amount of power based on the combustible material you put in. They also automatically distribute power to adjacent blocks."]
			old: ["These &8Coal Generators&r are some of the easiest generators to make.\\n\\nThey are very simple to use and create a decent amount of power based on the combustible material you put in. They also automatically distributes power to adjacent blocks."]
		}
		quest.1EECA19DF9CF6A0C.quest_desc: {
			new: ["Flux Dust can also be automated using &6XyCraft&r!\\n\\nPlace crying obsidian on bedrock, surround the crystal block with 4 obsidian on all sides and place the extractor on top.\\nThen just place a storage on top of the extractor and you're done!"]
			old: ["Flux Dust can also be automated using &6XyCraft&r!\\n\\nPlace a charged redstone crystal block on bedrock, surround the crystal block with 4 obsidian on all sides and place the extractor on top.\\nThen just place a storage on top of the extractor and you're done!"]
		}
		quest.0BB42C5861B22D32.title: {
			new: "&9Excessive Utilities: &zRainbow Generator"
			old: "&9Industrial Foregoing: &bMycelial Reactor"
		}
		quest.2D4749DF9642F334.quest_desc: {
			new: ["The &eDyson Cube&r is the ultimate power source, producing an insane &l&a100MFE/t&r&r!\\n\\nSet up an &eEM Rail Ejector Controller&r to launch &bSolar Sails&r and &bBeams&r into orbit around the Sun. You can input items &bautomatically&r through the center of the bottom face (you’ll definitely need automation to reach maximum power output). Unfortunately, it &ocannot fire&r at midday, at night, or during rain.\\n\\nTo collect that glorious energy, build a &bRay Receiver Controller&r. It outputs power from the center of its bottom face but &ocannot receive power&r during &enight&r or &erain&r.\\n\\nYou can &epackage&r beams and sails into bundles for faster launches, which is much easier than sending them one by one.\\n\\nFor maximum output, you’ll need to send &c833,333&r beams and &c4,999,998&r sails into orbit, which is quite a lot.\\n\\nBefore you start scaling up to that level, make sure you’ve got some &arobust resource generation&r in place."]
			old: [
				"The &eDyson Cube&r is the ultimate power source, producing an insane &l&a1GFE/t&r&r!"
				""
				"Set up an &eEM Rail Ejector Controller&r to launch &bSolar Sails&r and &bBeams&r into orbit around the Sun. You can input items &bautomatically&r through the center of the bottom face (you’ll definitely need automation to reach maximum power output). Unfortunately, it &ocannot fire&r at midday, at night, or during rain."
				""
				"To collect that glorious energy, build a &bRay Receiver Controller&r. It outputs power from the center of its bottom face but &ocannot receive power&r during &enight&r or &erain&r."
				""
				"You can &epackage&r beams and sails into bundles for faster launches, which is much easier than sending them one by one."
				""
				"For maximum output, you’ll need to send &c8,333,333&r beams and &c49,999,998&r sails into orbit, which is quite a lot."
				""
				"Before you start scaling up to that level, make sure you’ve got some &arobust resource generation&r in place."
			]
		}
		quest.0BB42C5861B22D32.quest_desc: {
			new: ["The &zRainbow Generator&r consists of all the Generators from &e&lExcessive Utilities&r working at the same time, and it produces a total of &a25MFE/t&r.\\n\\nAll sounds good, but you need to automate some stuff to get it working, see what each Generator consumes to work, and automate it, most things are simple, but others, not that much... &olooking at Disenchantment Generator&r."]
			old: ["The &bMycelial Reactor&r consists of all the Mycelial Generators working at the same time, near the reactor block, and it produces a total of &a25MFE/t&r.\\n\\nAll sounds good, but you need to automate some stuff to get it working, see what each Mycelial Generator consumes to work, and automate it, most things are simple, but others, not that much... &olooking at Disenchanting Mycelial Generator&r.\\n\\nBut after you get it all automated, you don't need to stop at one, you can make more reactors."]
		}
		quest.0BB42C5861B22D32.quest_subtitle: {
			new: "With your powers combined!"
			old: "It's not Yourcelial Reactor"
		}
		quest.43D83CFA824B0A70.quest_desc: {
			new: ["&9Mekanism&r has an end game power option that is...massively nerfed. The &dFusion Reactor&r can produce up to 400kRF/t, and if you want to learn how to build it, make sure to check out the &aMekanism: &dReactors&r quest chapter!"]
			old: ["&9Mekanism&r has an end game power option that is tough to beat. The &dFusion Reactor&r can produce up to 80MRF/t, and if you want to learn how to build it, make sure to check out the &aMekanism: &dReactors&r quest chapter!"]
		}
	}
	"chapters/industrial_foregoing.snbt": {
		image.2294CF2CFFFA8E1B.title: {
			new: "Latex Processing Unit"
			old: "Unidade de Processamento de Látex"
		}
		image.46F53AD18FF5C0E8.title: {
			new: "Block Placer"
			old: "Posicionador de Blocos"
		}
		image.542273876E978E47.title: {
			new: "Fluid Extractor"
			old: "Extrator de Fluidos"
		}
		image.1AC0CCC618E9CBE8.title: {
			new: "Fluid Extractor"
			old: "Extrator de Fluidos"
		}
		image.226296BE0F417E6D.title: {
			new: "Fluid Extractor"
			old: "Extrator de Fluidos"
		}
		quest.538186D01429F05F.quest_desc: {
			new: [
				"In this quest, we will be focusing on using AE2 to automate the &cPotion Brewer&r. First, build a setup like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/potionbrewerdemonstration.png width:175 height:200 align:center}"
				"(The Creative Energy Cell serves as a placeholder for your main network)"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"We'll need either an &9Export Bus&r or an &9Interface&r to fill the &cPotion Brewer&r with &1Water&r and &6Blaze Powder&r. The &6Blaze Powder&r will be used as fuel. Do not provide bottles yet, as they will fill your network with Water Bottles."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The next step will be to get an"
				"&5Advanced Pattern Provider&r. Check the Extended \\& Advanced AE chapter to learn more about how to use it. Next, we'll need to encode a pattern. An example will be to brew a &4Potion of Healing&r, focused on Royal Treats for Modular Bees. Encode the pattern like so: 3 Glass Bottles, 1 Nether Wart, 1 Glistering Melon Slice, to produce 3 &4Potions of Healing&r. We'll be using both of the &5Advanced Provider&r's special abilities here. First is its ability to send items to a specific side. We'll be using this to send Glass Bottles to the TOP side of the machine. Use the &5Advanced Pattern Encoder&r to encode the pattern, like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/advanced_pattern.png width:200 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Next, we need to enable Filtered Import on the &5Advanced Provider&r. This will make it so that the &5Advanced Provider&r only accepts items that match currently active crafting jobs. This means it won't accept potions prematurely. You can also add Processing Addons to aid with this, especially with large enough crafting jobs that may use that same provider.\\n\\nLastly, you'll have to configure the sides of the Potion Brewer like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/blaze_input.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/bottle_input.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/brewing_input.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/output.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"If you're using the &9Interface&r method, configure the sides like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/blaze_input_for_interface.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/water_for_interface.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Optionally, you can place a Flat Transfer Node between the &5Advanced Provider&r and the &cBrewer&r.\\n\\nIf you're still confused by this setup, or would rather watch a video, check out the video I have linked here, from ChosenArchitect:"
				"{\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://youtu.be/DOW4xkxqp6g?si=paZ2xFKyycPumqaS&t=427\"},\"color\":\"blue\",\"text\":\"VIDEO LINK HERE\",\"underlined\":true} "
			]
			old: [
				"In this quest, we will be focusing on using AE2 to automate the &cPotion Brewer&r. First, build a setup like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/potionbrewerdemonstration.png width:175 height:200 align:center}"
				"(The Creative Energy Cell serves as a placeholder for your main network)"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"We'll need either an &9Export Bus&r or an &9Interface&r to fill the &cPotion Brewer&r with &1Water&r and &6Blaze Powder&r. The &6Blaze Powder&r will be used as fuel. Do not provide bottles yet, as they will fill your network with Water Bottles."
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The next step will be to get an"
				"&5Advanced Pattern Provider&r. Check the Extended \\& Advanced AE chapter to learn more about how to use it. Next, we'll need to encode a pattern. An example will be to brew a &4Potion of Healing&r, focused on Royal Treats for Modular Bees. Encode the pattern like so: 3 Glass Bottles, 1 Nether Wart, 1 Glistering Melon Slice, to produce 3 &4Potions of Healing&r. We'll be using both of the &5Advanced Provider&r's special abilities here. First is its ability to send items to a specific side. We'll be using this to send Glass Bottles to the TOP side of the machine. Use the &5Advanced Pattern Encoder&r to encode the pattern, like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/advanced_pattern.png width:200 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Next, we need to enable Filtered Import on the &5Advanced Provider&r. This will make it so that the &5Advanced Provider&r only accepts items that match currently active crafting jobs. This means it won't accept potions prematurely. You can also add Processing Addons to aid with this, especially with large enough crafting jobs that may use that same provider.\\n\\nLastly, you'll have to configure the sides of the Potion Brewer like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/blaze_input.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/bottle_input.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/brewing_input.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/output.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"If you're using the &9Interface&r method, configure the sides like so:"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/blaze_input_for_interface.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{image:atm:textures/questpics/industrialforegoing/water_for_interface.png width:125 height:100 align:center}"
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Optionally, you can place a Transfer Label between the &5Advanced Provider&r and the &cBrewer&r.\\n\\nIf you're still confused by this setup, or would rather watch a video, check out the video I have linked here, from ChosenArchitect:"
				"{\"clickEvent\":{\"action\":\"open_url\",\"value\":\"https://youtu.be/DOW4xkxqp6g?si=paZ2xFKyycPumqaS&t=427\"},\"color\":\"blue\",\"text\":\"VIDEO LINK HERE\",\"underlined\":true} "
			]
		}
		image.362BDD0CB412D079.title: {
			new: "BucketSt's Industrial Foregoing Video"
			old: "Vídeo de Industrial Foregoing do BucketSt"
		}
	}
	"chapters/welcome.snbt": {
